% The customs background (lpsPlus docs/strategy/FactsBackground.md §6.1):
% the principal use of a plastics article, presumed from the name that a
% listing gives the article, as a customs text names the article. Each word
% is a name that the tariff's Chapter 39 (headings 3923, 3924 and 3926, their
% subheadings and statistical lines, and subheading note 5) or a US Customs
% ruling gives to an article of a use that the rules of Chapter 39 read
% (table uses). A name that two texts give to two uses (buckets and pails;
% handles and knobs) gives the two uses as alternatives.
%
% The value "other use" is for the articles that the tariff names under
% "Other" of 3926.90, and the articles that the rulings put there: their
% principal use is none of the uses that the rules read.
%
% Left out, because they name a legal category and not a thing a seller
% names: household articles, hygienic or toilet articles, clothing
% accessories, builders' ware. Left out, because a seller uses the word for
% another thing: case, cap, caps, seal, seals, belt, scarf, runner, panel.
%
% Used only to read facts from a text (language reference §14.5).

the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the principal use of *a good* is *a use*.

the templates are:
    *a thing* is called *a name*; undefined.
    the field *a field* of *a thing* reads *a value*; undefined.
    *a name* is a word for the use *a use*.
    *a field* is a field that names the kind.
    the principal use of *a good* is *a use*.

