% a classification controlled by use is decided by the principal use; the
% name of an article tells its use, as the tariff names its articles
rule use_by_name with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Tableware, kitchenware, other household articles and hygienic":
the principal use of a good is a use
    if the good is called a name
    and the name is a word for the use the use.

rule use_by_field with provenance the listing format,
        confer "Item Type (64 listings): the kind of product in the seller's words":
the principal use of a good is a use
    if the field a field of the good reads a value
    and the field is a field that names the kind
    and the value is a word for the use the use.

scenario plate is:
    plate one is called "plates".
    frame is called "picture frame".
    gloves is called "gloves".
    album is called "photo album".
    the field "item type" of figure reads "statuette".
    the field "type" of sack one reads "plastic bag".
    pail one is called "pail".
    uses expects answers ["the principal use of plate one is table use", "the principal use of frame is household use", "the principal use of gloves is apparel", "the principal use of album is other use", "the principal use of figure is ornament", "the principal use of sack one is packing of goods", "the principal use of pail one is packing of goods", "the principal use of pail one is other use"].

query uses is:
    the principal use of which good is which use.
